Z||000000||sdm1964||02-22-2000||09:09 PM||||I noticed an exaust leak this morning. I thought it a loosebolt at the flang, WRONG broken bolt on flange, After hours of fighting with the car i finally got the exaust manifold out, STILL BAD NEWS, cracked manifold and found a loose bolt holding the manifold on. OK now to the question, it took me forever to get the bolt off by the air compressor, lucky it was a little loose. How do i get the bolt back in? do i have to loosen or take off the compressor to get it back in and tight, of course it is the back manifold. Good news, i got a 600.00 bonus from work, now lets see new tires, shocks, struts and a weekend in daytona looking at all those fine fiero's, I guess the day was not a total loss, better today than on the road,<BR>thanks    Stephen<BR>ps. 85 GT with v-6<p>[This message has been edited by sdm1964 (edited 02-22-2000).]||||reg||1
