Z||000005||AL||02-23-2000||01:49 AM||||ok guys ijust finished replacing my manifold and this is how i took it off. first take the two bolts that hold the throtle and cruise cable off, o disconnect the linkage first then the bolts.move the wires and hook them to the plenum, then take the take off the shroud that connects the air filter to the throtle body, next take the two bolts off  the y pipe and the manifold, now climb into the trunk ley on the plenum and use a ratchet and a long socket size13 unscrew all bolts. now the bolt that is under the manifold next to the a/c with your left hand use a 13 mil wrench and take it out, it's a little pain in the butt, but it is better then taking brackets out,once you'v taken it out, proceed with installing the new manifold. the bolt that is a pain, you are going to put it in, using your two fingers and gliding the bolt from one side of the manifold and trying to catch it with the other finger(thumb and finger). once you've put it in tighten all bolts. you have to loosen the other pipe that connects to the other manifold, in order to alighn the other pipe to the other manifold, once you've done this tighten the pipe of the manifold that you just put in and then tighten the other side and it should work fine. i hope you have understood this, it's not that hard, good luck, AL.  ||||reg||14
